=======================================
   MAIN COMPONENTS INSIDE A DESKTOP PC
========================================

1. Motherboard
   The main circuit board that connects all PC components.
   It allows the CPU, RAM, storage and other devices to communicate.

2. CPU (Processor)
   The main processing unit of the computer.
   It handles instructions and performs calculations.

3. RAM (Memory)
   Temporarily stores data and programs currently in use.
   It helps the computer handle multiple tasks smoothly.

4. Motherboard Chipset
   Manages communication between the CPU, storage, USB devices and hardware.
   It controls many features and connections on the motherboard.

5. Power Supply Unit (PSU)
   Supplies electrical power to all PC components.
   It converts AC power into the required DC power.

6. GPU (Graphics Card)
   Processes images, videos and graphics for the display.
   It is useful for gaming, video editing and graphics-heavy tasks.

7. Storage Drive (HDD/SSD)
   Stores the operating system, applications and personal files.
   HDDs use magnetic disks, while SSDs use flash memory.

8. SATA Cable
   Connects SATA storage drives to the motherboard.
   It transfers data between the storage drive and motherboard.

9. CPU Cooler
   Removes heat produced by the processor.
   It usually consists of a heatsink and a fan.

10. Case Fans
    Move air through the cabinet to control temperature.
    They help keep the internal components cool.

11. CMOS Battery
    Helps maintain the system clock and BIOS/UEFI settings.
    It provides power when the PC is turned off.

12. Expansion Cards
    Installed in PCIe slots to add extra features.
    Examples include Wi-Fi, sound and capture cards.

13. Cables and Connectors
    Connect the power supply, storage drives, fans and other components.
    They provide power and allow components to communicate.

